    "/api/method/frappe.desk.doctype.number_card.number_card.get_result": {
      "post": {
        "summary": "FITIT Overview number card value (one call per card)",
        "description": "Called by the FITIT Overview workspace (/desk/selling/fitit-overview). Request body is form-encoded; hooks read it as ctx.request['form'] with JSON values already decoded. Fields: doc (the Number Card: name, label, function Sum|Count, document_type, aggregate_function_based_on, filters_json), filters (list of [doctype, field, op, value]). Response {\"message\": <number>} is the value the card shows. Pick the card by ctx.request['form']['doc']['name'], one of: FITIT Sales revenue, FITIT Sales orders, FITIT Active customers, FITIT Amount to collect, FITIT Sales leads, FITIT Suppliers, FITIT Products & services, FITIT Paid invoices. No dry run: use ctx.request.get('form', {}) / ctx.request.get('query', {}) so an empty ctx.request is safe. ",
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "OK",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "example": {
                  "message": 8390.0
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/api/method/frappe.desk.doctype.dashboard_chart.dashboard_chart.get": {
      "post": {
        "summary": "FITIT Overview chart data (one call per chart)",
        "description": "Called by the FITIT Overview workspace (/desk/selling/fitit-overview). Request body is form-encoded; hooks read it as ctx.request['form'] with JSON values already decoded. Fields: chart_name, filters, timespan, time_interval, from_date, to_date. Response {\"message\": {\"labels\": [...], \"datasets\": [{\"name\", \"values\": [...]}]}}. Pick the chart by ctx.request['form']['chart_name'], one of: FITIT Sales Performance, FITIT Invoice Status, FITIT Revenue by Customer. No dry run: use ctx.request.get('form', {}) / ctx.request.get('query', {}) so an empty ctx.request is safe. ",
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "OK",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "example": {
                  "message": {
                    "labels": [
                      "25-09-2026",
                      "26-09-2026"
                    ],
                    "datasets": [
                      {
                        "name": "FITIT Sales Performance",
                        "values": [
                          368.0,
                          324.0
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/api/method/frappe.desk.form.load.getdoc": {
      "get": {
        "summary": "Load one document (the overview loads each Number Card and Dashboard Chart through it)",
        "description": "Called by the FITIT Overview workspace (/desk/selling/fitit-overview). Query: doctype, name (e.g. doctype=Number Card&name=FITIT Sales orders), read as ctx.request['query']. Response {\"docs\": [{name, label, function, document_type, aggregate_function_based_on, filters_json, color, ...}], \"docinfo\": {...}}. ERPNext computes the card value from docs[0].filters_json (a JSON string of [doctype, field, op, value] lists) and function, so a hook here changes what a card counts or sums, e.g. only Aurora Clinic orders on FITIT Sales orders: filters_json[:-1] + ', [\"Sales Order\", \"customer\", \"=\", \"FITIT Aurora Clinic\"]]'. The card title comes from the workspace layout and cannot be changed (renaming it in get_desktop_page hides the card). Customer names start with 'FITIT ' (FITIT Aurora Clinic, FITIT Brisa Architecture, FITIT Cedar Academy). No dry run: use ctx.request.get('form', {}) / ctx.request.get('query', {}) so an empty ctx.request is safe. ",
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "OK",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "example": {
                  "docs": [
                    {
                      "name": "FITIT Sales orders",
                      "label": "Sales orders",
                      "function": "Count",
                      "document_type": "Sales Order",
                      "filters_json": "[[\"Sales Order\", \"name\", \"like\", \"FITIT%\"], [\"Sales Order\", \"docstatus\", \"=\", 1]]"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
